# Synchronous vs Asynchronous Execution ⏳

- **Synchronous (Blocking):** Code runs line by line in order. Each line must finish before the next line can begin. Long operations freeze the browser!
- **Asynchronous (Non-Blocking):** Long-running operations (API requests, timers) run in the background. When ready, their callback runs, allowing other code to continue uninterrupted!

```javascript
console.log("1. Starting task");

setTimeout(() => {
  console.log("2. Timer finished (after 100ms)");
}, 100);

console.log("3. Continuing execution without waiting!");
```

