# Microtasks vs Macrotasks Execution Order ⏱️

Look at this classic JavaScript interview question:

```javascript
console.log("1. Synchronous");

setTimeout(() => {
  console.log("2. Macrotask (setTimeout)");
}, 0);

Promise.resolve().then(() => {
  console.log("3. Microtask (Promise)");
});

console.log("4. Synchronous");
```

## Output:
`1. Synchronous` -> `4. Synchronous` -> `3. Microtask` -> `2. Macrotask`!
Microtasks (Promises) always run before Macrotasks (`setTimeout`).

